# The artefacts under `include/` are compared byte for byte, not merely read: `build.rs` regenerates
# them on every build, and a rebuild that leaves the working tree dirty turns "the ABI changed" into
# something a developer sees after changing nothing. Their generator writes LF, so LF is what a
# checkout has to leave behind, on every platform.
#
# `cbindgen.toml` is here for the same reason at one remove: its `header` string is embedded in the
# generated header verbatim, so a CR in the checkout is a CR in the artefact.
cbindgen.toml text eol=lf
include/** text eol=lf
